From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 19:34:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 10952/11362] Tell task authors which verdict_class costs three
 attempts

The verdict_class enum has one member the conductor re-runs, partial, and five
that are terminal. The planner prompt listed the enum and never said so, leaving
authors to pick a class without knowing which one ends in a retirement.

On 2026-09-03 both the v605 and v608 capstones declared partial over milestones
whose upstream tasks had been cascade-blocked -- v608 lost ten of twelve tasks to
one root. Each burned three attempts on three identical artifacts and was
retired. Two milestones lost their capstone for describing their inputs
accurately with the wrong class, and blocked was available and correct both
times.

The prompt now states that partial asserts the author's OWN work is unfinished
and invites a retry, that external incompleteness -- upstream retired,
gate-blocked or absent -- must be declared blocked with the upstream and failing
field named, and it carries the incident so the rule is not edited away by
someone who does not know its price.

Deliberately a prompt fix and not a guard change. _verdict_is_untrustworthy has
been enum-first since REQ-CONDUCTOR-VERDICT-2 and retrying a partial is the
right default, because a partial result usually is worth another attempt. My own
earlier claim that the guard punished honest self-classification was wrong,
retracted in ops/known-issues.md, and this spec entry says not to act on it.

REQ-CONDUCTOR-VERDICT-4 with one scenario. Six tests, mutation-proven by
deleting the guidance, which takes all six RED, then restoring byte-identically
for GREEN.

